Row Level Security (RLS) has been enabled on all five tables (Users, Channels, Posts, Comments, Channel Moderators) with the following policies implemented according to your requirements:

1. Users Table:
- SELECT: Users can read all public profiles.
- UPDATE: Users can only update their own profile.
- DELETE: Users can only delete their own account.

2. Channels Table:
- SELECT: Everyone can read public channels.
- INSERT: Authenticated users can create channels.
- UPDATE: Only channel owners can update channels.
- DELETE: Only channel owners can delete channels.

3. Posts Table:
- SELECT: Users can read posts only in accessible channels.
- INSERT: Authenticated users can create posts.
- UPDATE: Post authors, channel moderators, or owners can update posts.
- DELETE: Post authors, channel moderators, or owners can delete posts.

4. Comments Table:
- SELECT: Users can read comments on accessible posts.
- INSERT: Authenticated users can comment on accessible posts.
- UPDATE: Comment authors, post authors, moderators, or owners can update comments.
- DELETE: Comment authors, post authors, moderators, or owners can delete comments.

5. Channel Moderators Table:
- SELECT: Users can see moderator lists.
- INSERT: Only channel owners can add moderators.
- DELETE: Channel owners can remove moderators; moderators can remove themselves.

All policies use the helper functions as required, and session context handling is integrated with the function `app_current_user_id()`.

